LeakSanitizer: small one-shot leaks on error/lookup paths (first sanitise CI
runs on the poseidon runners; the lane had never executed before).

INVENTORY (repro: docker run ... ci/debian-gcc:latest
  'make -k build SANITIZE=yes BUILD=debug && make -k -C tests test SANITIZE=yes BUILD=debug'):
- string_cstring results passed to the ERROR/TYPE_ERROR macros leak BY DESIGN:
  error()/type_error() format the message then longjmp, so the malloc'd
  argument is never freed (boerror.c:145-146 frames; the same pattern exists
  across eval.c/kernel.c error paths — e.g. the v1.8.32
  "Undefined function: ~A" sites).  8-80 bytes ONCE per signalled error.
  FIX SKETCH: have type_error()/error() accept Ref arguments and do their own
  string_cstring+free internally (or a %s-from-Ref format helper), so callers
  stop pre-converting.
- printer.c current_readtable_case / current_print_case leaked their case-
  keyword cstring per call — FIXED in the same commit (free after strcmp).
8 of 42 suites currently fail the leak check (13-80 bytes each, error-path
one-shots).  sanitise:debian-gcc is allow_failure until the error-path
pattern is reworked; the job still runs and reports, so NEW leak classes stay
visible in its log.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIXED (v1.8.44) — the sanitise lane is CLEAN; its allow_failure is removed.

The shared fix: boerror gains STRING_STATIC_CSTR(string) — the string's bytes
in a static ROTATING buffer (8 slots x 256, truncating) — for every C-string
that feeds a longjmp-ing ERROR/TYPE_ERROR/FATAL message or a fire-and-forget
debug print: nothing malloc'd, nothing to leak.

Converted: type_error's own GOT/EXPECTED names (it leaked on every SIGNALLED
type error); kernel_ERROR's report + condition-class name; every
ERROR(...string_cstring...) argument across eval.c (11 sites incl. the
v1.8.32 "Undefined function"), bytecode.c (vm_symbol_function, cf_name_cstr),
arithmetic.c (3), conditions.c (3), structure.c, and the debug.c dump helpers.
Plain missing frees fixed where the path RETURNS normally: printer.c
print_name_escaped + invert_scan (leaked the name cstring on EVERY printed
symbol), kernel_PARSE_FLOAT, and the vm_call_frame_bindings '&'-check in the
backtrace builder.

VERIFIED in the CI image (registry.gitlab.com/bocl/bocl/ci/debian-gcc):
make build SANITIZE=yes + the full 42-suite run — ZERO LeakSanitizer reports,
status 0 (was 8 failing suites).  Plain build green locally.
